\subsection{Paginating across multiple result pages}\label{Pagination}

Many LADOK endpoints return a fixed-size page of results plus a
[[TotaltAntalPoster]] field giving the total count.  If a caller wants
\emph{all} results --- e.g.\ all course rounds for a course code, all
participants in a programme round, all examination occasions for a
course --- they have to walk every page.

The naive workaround is to ask for an enormous [[limit]] (we used 400
in places below).  That stops working the moment a query genuinely
crosses the limit, and it fails silently: the caller gets the first 400
items and never finds out the rest exist.  We instead provide a
[[_all_pages]] helper that walks pages until the running total matches
the server's [[TotaltAntalPoster]], so the caller-facing methods can
stay parameterless and always return the complete list.

The helper takes a [[request_fn(page, limit)]] callable rather than a
URL and content-type pair.  This lets it work with both [[get_query]]
(URL query-string pagination) and [[put_query]] (body-field
pagination, used by [[occasion_results_JSON]]) without having to
duplicate the looping logic --- the closure captures whatever
endpoint-specific machinery the caller needs.

If the response is missing either [[key]] or [[TotaltAntalPoster]], we
raise [[LadokAPIError]] in the same \enquote{fail loud on schema
drift} style as the rest of this module: a paginated endpoint that
suddenly stops returning [[TotaltAntalPoster]] is exactly the kind of
change the caller needs to see, not silently swallow.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def _all_pages(self,
               request_fn: Callable[[int, int], dict],
               key: str = "Resultat",
               page_size: int = 400) -> list:
  """Concatenate every page of a paginated LADOK endpoint.

  request_fn(page, limit) must return the raw response dict
  containing `key` (a list of items) and 'TotaltAntalPoster' (total
  number of items across all pages, 1-based page numbering).

  Returns the flat list of items.  Raises LadokAPIError if any page
  is missing the expected keys.
  """
  items = []
  page = 1
  while True:
    data = request_fn(page, page_size)
    try:
      chunk = data[key]
      total = data["TotaltAntalPoster"]
    except KeyError as err:
      err.add_note(f"Response data: {data}")
      raise LadokAPIError(
        f"Paginated response missing '{key}' or "
        f"'TotaltAntalPoster' on page {page}"
      ) from err
    items.extend(chunk)
    if len(items) >= total or not chunk:
      return items
    page += 1
@


\section{Cleaning data for printing}

We sometimes want to print the data, for instance, example output in this 
document.
For this reason we introduce some cleaning functions.
These recursively transcends the JSON structure removing the data that should 
be removed.
<<functions>>=
def clean_data(json_obj: dict | list) -> dict | list:
  """
  Clean a JSON object by removing internal links and pseudonymizing personal data.

  Args:
      json_obj (dict or list): The JSON data to clean.

  Returns:
      dict or list: The cleaned JSON object.
  """
  remove_links(json_obj)
  pseudonymize(json_obj)
  return json_obj
@

The [[remove_links]] functions removes the [[link]] key--value pairs.
The [[link]] values contains URLs for all requests that data are based on.
<<functions>>=
def remove_links(json_obj: dict | list) -> None:
  """
  Recursively removes all "link" keys and values
  """
  if isinstance(json_obj, dict):
    if "link" in json_obj:
      json_obj.pop("link")
    for key, value in json_obj.items():
      remove_links(value)
  elif isinstance(json_obj, list):
    for item in json_obj:
      remove_links(item)
@

The [[pseudonymize]] function replaces names and personnummer with dummy 
entries.
<<functions>>=
def pseudonymize(json_obj: dict | list) -> None:
  """
  Recursively pseudonymizes a JSON data record
  """
  if isinstance(json_obj, dict):
    if "Fornamn" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Fornamn"] = "Student"
    if "Efternamn" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Efternamn"] = "Studentzadeh"
    if "Personnummer" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Personnummer"] = "191234561234"
    if "Epostadress" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Epostadress"] = "user@domain.se"
    if "Anvandarnamn" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Anvandarnamn"] = "user@domain.se"
    if "Utdelningsadress" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Utdelningsadress"] = "Stora vägen 1"
    if "Postnummer" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Postnummer"] = "12345"
    if "Postort" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Postort"] = "Byn"
    if "Telefonnummer" in json_obj:
      json_obj["Telefonnummer"] = "0701234567"
    for value in json_obj.values():
      pseudonymize(value)
  elif isinstance(json_obj, list):
    for item in json_obj:
      pseudonymize(item)
