\section{[[student_result_history_JSON]]}

The preceding methods answer the question ``who sat which exam and what
did they get?''\@ from the perspective of an \emph{occasion}.  But for
analysing student progress we often need the opposite perspective: given
a student, what is their \emph{complete} result history across every
course and every attempt?

The LADOK~GUI presents exactly this on a student's historik~(history)
tab.  Discovering the underlying endpoint took a detour through the
hypermedia links embedded in the [[resultatuppfoljning/sok]] response:
each [[Student]] object carries a link with relation
[[resultat/historik]] pointing to
[[/resultat/internal/historik/student/{uid}]].

\subsection*{Structure of the response}

The endpoint returns a single key [[Historikposter]], a flat list of
result events ordered newest-first.  Each event captures one grade
action and contains:

\begin{description}
\item[[[Sammanfattning]]] A human-readable summary in Swedish and
  English, e.g.\ ``Modern fysik~4.0~hp SH1014 / Tentamen~4.0~hp TEN1''.
  Course-level entries (finalization of a whole course) have no
  slash-separated component; component-level entries do.
\item[[[Examinationsdatum]]] The date the examination took place.
\item[[[BetyggradID]]] Numeric identifier of the grade; combine with
  [[BetygsskalaID]] to resolve the letter code (A--F, P/F, etc.).
\item[[[AvserOmfattning]]] Credits the result covers (0.0 for
  course-level finalization entries).
\item[[[Handelse]]] The event type: [[skapad]]~(created),
  [[borttagen]]~(deleted/retracted), or [[rattad]]~(corrected).
\item[[[Historiktyp]]] Always [[resultat.domain.historiktyp.resultat]]
  for grade results.
\item[[[Attestant]], [[Beslutsfattare]]] Who certified and who decided
  the grade.
\item[[[link]]] Contains a [[historik/pakurs]] relation linking to the
  per-course variant of this endpoint
  ([[historik/student/{uid}/kurs/{kurs\_uid}]]).
\end{description}

Crucially, \emph{all} attempts appear, including failed ones and
subsequently corrected results.  A student who failed TEN1 in January
2025 and passed in January 2026 will have two separate entries for
TEN1~--- one with the failing grade and one with the passing grade~---
plus a third entry for the course-level finalization that only appears
once the student has passed.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def student_result_history_JSON(self, student_uid: str) -> list:
  """Return all result history events for a student.

  Uses GET /resultat/internal/historik/student/{uid}.

  Returns a list of Historikposter (history events) covering every
  course and component the student has received a grade in, newest
  first.  All attempts are included --- failed grades, corrected
  results, and retracted entries appear alongside passing grades.
  """
  data = self.get_query(
    f"/resultat/internal/historik/student/{student_uid}")
  try:
    return data["Historikposter"]
  except KeyError as err:
    err.add_note(f"Response data: {data}")
    raise LadokAPIError(
      f"Unexpected response format when fetching result history "
      f"for student {student_uid}: missing 'Historikposter' key"
    ) from err
@

We test with a student who has two TEN1 entries for SH1014: a failing
grade from January~2025 and a passing~C from January~2026.
<<test functions>>=
def test_student_result_history_JSON() -> None:
  history = ladok.student_result_history_JSON(SH1014_retake_student_uid)
  assert isinstance(history, list)
  assert len(history) > 0
  # Every entry must have the core fields
  for entry in history:
    assert "Sammanfattning" in entry
    assert "Examinationsdatum" in entry
    assert "Historiktyp" in entry
    assert "Handelse" in entry
  # Verify that multiple SH1014/TEN1 attempts are present
  sh1014_ten1 = [
    e for e in history
    if "SH1014" in e.get("Sammanfattning", {}).get("sv", "")
    and "TEN1" in e.get("Sammanfattning", {}).get("sv", "")
  ]
  assert len(sh1014_ten1) >= 2, (
    f"Expected at least 2 SH1014/TEN1 entries (F then C), got {len(sh1014_ten1)}"
  )
