\section{[[grade_scales_all_text]]}

[[grade_scales_JSON]] (\cref{GradeScalesJSON}) returns the standard
grade scales the LADOK JSON variant exposes --- but not all of them.
Empirically, the same endpoint
[[/kataloginformation/internal/grunddata/betygsskala]] queried with an
XML [[Accept]] header returns a strictly larger set: it includes
institution-specific scales such as KTH's seven-point A--F scale that
the JSON variant omits.  Why the JSON representation filters and the
XML one doesn't is undocumented, and the situation may change ---
future maintainers should periodically retry the JSON endpoint and
collapse the two methods into one if the asymmetry goes away.

We deliberately return the raw response \emph{text} rather than parse
the XML here.  Parsing belongs in the caller because (a) consumers of
this method already need to walk a heterogeneous mix of standard and
institution-specific scales, and (b) we don't want to add an
[[xml.etree]] dependency to this module just to expose one endpoint
variant.  The thin [[get_query_text]] helper carries the request,
re-using [[get_query]]'s session and error mapping so a failure here
raises the same [[LadokServerError]] / [[LadokAPIError]] callers
already handle.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def grade_scales_all_text(self) -> str:
  """Fetch ALL grade scales as raw XML, including institution-specific ones.

  Uses GET /kataloginformation/internal/grunddata/betygsskala with an
  explicit Accept: application/xml header.  Without this, the server
  returns JSON (the standard 17-scale subset), which omits institution-
  specific scales such as KTH's A--F scale.

  Returns the raw XML response text for the caller to parse.  Use
  grade_scales_JSON() if you only need the standard subset and want
  it pre-parsed.
  """
  return self.get_query_text(
    "/kataloginformation/internal/grunddata/betygsskala",
    accept="application/xml, text/xml;q=0.9, */*;q=0.1",
  )
@

We sanity-check that the response is XML rather than empty or HTML
(an HTML response would indicate the session has been redirected to a
login page, which [[get_query_text]] doesn't otherwise detect).

<<test functions>>=
def test_grade_scales_all_text() -> None:
  text = ladok.grade_scales_all_text()
  assert text
  assert "<?xml" in text or "<betygsskala" in text.lower() \
      or "<Betygsskala" in text
@

\section{Shared helper: [[_utbildningstillfalle_JSON]]}

In LADOK, [[utbildningstillfalle]] (\enquote{education round}) is the
umbrella term that covers both \emph{course} rounds
([[kurstillfalle]]) and \emph{programme} rounds
([[kurspaketeringstillfalle]]) --- both kinds are stored as
[[utbildningstillfalle]] records by the
[[utbildningsinformation]] service, and one endpoint serves both:
\[
  \texttt{GET /utbildningsinformation/internal/utbildningstillfalle/\{uid\}}.
\]
The two public wrappers below ([[program_round_by_uid_JSON]] and
[[course_round_utbildningsinformation_JSON]]) call this same endpoint;
their value is in the \emph{intent} they expose at the call site --- a
reader who sees [[program_round_by_uid_JSON(uid)]] knows the caller
expects programme-round metadata, not just \enquote{some
utbildningstillfälle record}.  We keep the wrappers thin so the URL
and Accept-header live in exactly one place; if LADOK ever
restructures this endpoint, only the helper changes.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def _utbildningstillfalle_JSON(self, uid: str) -> dict:
  """Fetch an utbildningstillfalle record (course or programme round).

  Internal helper.  Uses GET
  /utbildningsinformation/internal/utbildningstillfalle/{uid}.

  Most callers should use the intent-revealing wrappers
  program_round_by_uid_JSON or course_round_utbildningsinformation_JSON
  instead of calling this directly.
  """
  return self.get_query(
    f"/utbildningsinformation/internal/utbildningstillfalle/{uid}",
    "application/vnd.ladok-utbildningsinformation+json",
  )
@


