\section{[[student_course_round_participations_JSON]]}

Which course rounds does a student participate in?  LADOK can answer
that question in two ways, and the two answers differ both in scope and
in who is allowed to ask.  This section and the two that follow cover
the pair of views and the method that unifies them:
\begin{description}
\item[{[[student_course_round_participations_JSON]]}] the dedicated
  participations view --- narrow but permission-gated (this section);
\item[{[[student_course_registrations_JSON]]}] every registration the
  student ever had --- wide but available to everyone;
\item[{[[student_course_participations_JSON]]}] tries the narrow view
  first and falls back to the wide one.
\end{description}

The dedicated
[[/studiedeltagande/internal/deltagare/kurstillfalle/student/{uid}]]
endpoint corresponds to the participation view in the LADOK GUI: the
course rounds the student currently takes part in.  It is
permission-gated, however.  For an account with programme-level roles
it works --- Christian Ohm (\enquote{cohm}), who contributed this
method in pull request \#129, uses it in production for programme
administration.  For an ordinary teacher's account LADOK answers
[[404 Not Found]], in the test environment \emph{and} in production
(verified against production on 2026-08-04).  A 404 surfaces as
[[LadokAPIError]] from [[get_query]], or [[LadokServerError]] when the
response body carries a [[Meddelande]].

Because we cannot exercise this endpoint without those roles, we keep
the implementation exactly as contributed and tested by its author ---
including the lenient unwrapping that accepts both response shapes he
observed rather than failing loudly on either.  Rewriting it to match
the module's fail-loud style would discard the only verification we
have.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def student_course_round_participations_JSON(self, student_uid: str) -> list:
  """Return all course-round participations for a student.

  Uses GET /studiedeltagande/internal/deltagare/kurstillfalle/student/{uid}.

  Requires programme-level Ladok roles; without them LADOK answers
  404 Not Found and this method raises a LadokError.

  Each item typically contains:
    - UtbildningstillfalleUID: the course round UUID
    - Utbildningsinformation.Utbildningskod: the course code
    - Status.Kod: participation status
  """
  data = self.get_query(
    f"/studiedeltagande/internal/deltagare/kurstillfalle/student/{student_uid}",
    "application/vnd.ladok-studiedeltagande+json",
  )
  return data.get("Tillfallesdeltaganden", data.get("Resultat", []))
@

