\section{[[student_course_registrations_JSON]]}

The view available to everyone is [[registrations_JSON]]: every
tillfällesdeltagande the student has ever had --- ongoing courses, but
also courses completed years ago, withdrawals, study breaks and
programme rounds.  Filtering it on
[[Utbildningsinformation.Utbildningstillfallestyp.Grundtyp]] being
[[KURS]] keeps exactly the course registrations.  That is a much wider
net than the previous section's participation view: one sampled student
had 45 course registrations of which only 5 were ongoing.

The width is sometimes the point --- the [[ladok program]] exporter
wants results from historical courses too --- and sometimes a problem:
discovering a cohort's \emph{current} courses through this view drags
in every course round any member ever touched.  So we let the caller
narrow the result by state.  Each registration summarizes its state in
[[TillstandKurs.Sammanfattattillstand]], a token like
[[studiedeltagande.domain.tillstandsdefinition.registrerad]] whose last
component is one of:
\begin{description}
\item[{[[registrerad]]}] ongoing --- registered but not yet finished;
\item[{[[avklarad]]}] completed;
\item[{[[aterbud]]}] the student withdrew before the round started;
\item[{[[avbrott]]}] the student broke off during the round.
\end{description}
The [[states]] parameter takes a set of these last components, so
passing [[{"registrerad"}]] reproduces the narrow \enquote{current
courses} view from data every account can read.  We compare only the
last dot-separated component; callers should not have to care about
the [[studiedeltagande.domain.tillstandsdefinition]] prefix.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def student_course_registrations_JSON(self, student_uid: str, /,
                                      states: set | None = None) -> list:
  """Return all course registrations for a student.

  Uses registrations_JSON() as the source and keeps only course
  entries.  This includes every registration the student ever had:
  completed courses, withdrawals and study breaks as well as ongoing
  courses.

  states: optional set of summarized states to keep, out of
    "registrerad" (ongoing), "avklarad" (completed), "aterbud"
    (withdrawal before start) and "avbrott" (break during the
    course).  None keeps everything.

  Each item typically contains:
    - Utbildningsinformation.UtbildningstillfalleUID: the course round UUID
    - Utbildningsinformation.Utbildningskod: the course code
    - TillstandKurs: participation state summary
  """
  registrations = []
  for registration in self.registrations_JSON(student_uid):
    try:
      grundtyp = registration["Utbildningsinformation"][
        "Utbildningstillfallestyp"]["Grundtyp"]
    except KeyError as err:
      err.add_note(f"Registration data: {registration}")
      raise LadokAPIError(
        f"Unexpected registration format when fetching course "
        f"registrations for student {student_uid}: missing "
        f"'Utbildningsinformation.Utbildningstillfallestyp.Grundtyp'"
      ) from err
    if grundtyp == "KURS":
      registrations.append(registration)
  if states is None:
    return registrations
  return filter_participations_by_state(registrations, states)
@

The state filter lives in a module-level function rather than inside
the method because [[student_course_participations_JSON]] must apply
the same narrowing to results from the permission-gated endpoint.  It
follows the module's fail-loud pattern: a missing state key raises
[[LadokAPIError]] with the offending entry attached instead of
silently dropping the entry --- silent dropping would make a schema
change look like a student without courses.

<<functions>>=
def filter_participations_by_state(participations: list,
                                   states: set) -> list:
  """Keep only participations whose summarized state is in states.

  states contains last components of
  TillstandKurs.Sammanfattattillstand values, e.g. "registrerad".
  Raises LadokAPIError if an entry lacks the state key.
  """
  kept = []
  for participation in participations:
    try:
      state = participation["TillstandKurs"]["Sammanfattattillstand"]
    except KeyError as err:
      err.add_note(f"Participation data: {participation}")
      raise LadokAPIError(
        "Unexpected participation format: missing "
        "'TillstandKurs.Sammanfattattillstand'") from err
    if state.rsplit(".", 1)[-1] in states:
      kept.append(participation)
  return kept
@

The retake student took SH1014 multiple times, so their course
registrations must contain at least one entry, and the [[Grundtyp]]
filter must hold for all of them.

