\section{[[student_course_participations_JSON]]}

Now we can unify the two views.  Callers of this method --- notably
programme portals iterating over a whole cohort --- want the student's
course participations, and prefer the narrow participation view
whenever their account can read it.  So we try
[[student_course_round_participations_JSON]] first and fall back to
[[student_course_registrations_JSON]].

We catch any [[LadokError]] rather than looking for a 404
specifically, because [[get_query]] collapses the HTTP status into the
message text of [[LadokAPIError]] or [[LadokServerError]].  For an
account with the required roles the endpoint works, so any error means
the narrow view is not available to this account and the wide view is
the best we can offer.

One failed probe per student would be wasteful --- a cohort import
makes this call hundreds of times --- so the first failure is
remembered on the session in
[[_course_round_participations_available]].  We read it with
[[getattr]] and a default of [[True]] because sessions are restored
from pickles ([[ladok3.cli]] caches them), and a session pickled by an
older version has no such attribute.

The [[states]] filter applies to whichever view produced the result.
On the fallback path the entries are registration objects, where the
filter is verified to work.  Whether the permission-gated view's
entries carry [[TillstandKurs]] we cannot observe from this account;
if they do not, the filter fails loudly with the entry attached, so a
privileged caller can report the actual shape rather than silently
receiving an empty list.  Note the placement of the filter outside the
[[try]]: a filter error must propagate, not masquerade as the endpoint
being unavailable and trigger the fallback.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def student_course_participations_JSON(self, student_uid: str, /,
                                       states: set | None = None) -> list:
  """Return all course-round participations for a student.

  Tries the dedicated participations view
  (student_course_round_participations_JSON(), which needs
  programme-level Ladok roles) and falls back to the registrations
  view (student_course_registrations_JSON(), available to everyone).
  Note that the fallback is wider: it includes completed and withdrawn
  registrations, not just current participations.

  states: optional set of summarized states to keep, see
    student_course_registrations_JSON().
  """
  if getattr(self, "_course_round_participations_available", True):
    try:
      participations = self.student_course_round_participations_JSON(
        student_uid)
    except LadokError:
      self._course_round_participations_available = False
    else:
      if states is None:
        return participations
      return filter_participations_by_state(participations, states)
  return self.student_course_registrations_JSON(student_uid,
                                                states=states)
@

In the test environment the maintainer's account lacks the programme
roles, so this test exercises the fallback path: the result must then
equal the registrations view, and a second call must give the same
answer as the first --- that is the capability cache at work.  For an
account where the narrow view works we can assert much less, only that
a list comes back.

<<test functions>>=
def test_student_course_participations_JSON() -> None:
  participations = ladok.student_course_participations_JSON(
    SH1014_retake_student_uid)
  assert isinstance(participations, list)
  again = ladok.student_course_participations_JSON(
    SH1014_retake_student_uid)
  assert again == participations
  if not getattr(ladok, "_course_round_participations_available", True):
    assert len(participations) > 0
    assert participations == ladok.student_course_registrations_JSON(
      SH1014_retake_student_uid)
